-- POWER BI DAX — enter EACH measure separately (Modeling > New measure).
-- Table name: Complaints; sourced using PowerBI_M_Cleaning.pq.
-- Source data are unique by Complaint ID and preserve timeliness blanks.

-- 1. Unique complaint count (used by all grouped product, year, month, issue, sub-product, sub-issue visuals)
Total Complaints = DISTINCTCOUNT('Complaints'[Complaint ID])

-- 2. Yes/No timeliness (do not convert blank to No)
Timely Yes = COALESCE(CALCULATE([Total Complaints], 'Complaints'[Timely response?] = "Yes"), 0)
Timely No = COALESCE(CALCULATE([Total Complaints], 'Complaints'[Timely response?] = "No"), 0)
Valid Timeliness Records = [Timely Yes] + [Timely No]
Recorded Timely Response % = DIVIDE([Timely Yes], [Valid Timeliness Records])
Excluded Timeliness Records = [Total Complaints] - [Valid Timeliness Records]

-- 3. In progress and response classification
In Progress = COALESCE(CALCULATE([Total Complaints], 'Complaints'[Company response to consumer] = "In progress"), 0)
Closed With Explanation = COALESCE(CALCULATE([Total Complaints], 'Complaints'[Company response to consumer] = "Closed with explanation"), 0)

-- 4. CFPB forwarding: 'Date received' means CFPB forwarded to company
Average Forwarding Days = AVERAGE('Complaints'[Forwarding Days])
Median Forwarding Days = MEDIAN('Complaints'[Forwarding Days])
Max Forwarding Days = MAX('Complaints'[Forwarding Days])
Forwarding More Than 25 Days = COALESCE(CALCULATE([Total Complaints], 'Complaints'[Forwarding Days] > 25), 0)
Same Day Forwarded = COALESCE(CALCULATE([Total Complaints], 'Complaints'[Forwarding Days] = 0), 0)

-- 5. Product share: retain other slicers (year etc.) but remove Product from denominator
Product Share % = DIVIDE([Total Complaints], CALCULATE([Total Complaints], REMOVEFILTERS('Complaints'[Product])))

-- 6. Annual YOY — place on a Year visual, not on a Month Start chart.
-- 2017/2023 incomplete; 2018 not compared against partial 2017.
Previous Full Year Complaints =
VAR SelectedYear = SELECTEDVALUE('Complaints'[Year])
RETURN
    IF(SelectedYear >= 2019 && SelectedYear <= 2022,
        CALCULATE([Total Complaints],
            REMOVEFILTERS('Complaints'[Year]),
            'Complaints'[Year] = SelectedYear - 1),
        BLANK())

Full Year YoY % =
VAR SelectedYear = SELECTEDVALUE('Complaints'[Year])
RETURN
    IF(SelectedYear >= 2019 && SelectedYear <= 2022,
        DIVIDE([Total Complaints] - [Previous Full Year Complaints], [Previous Full Year Complaints]),
        BLANK())

-- 7. Optional ranked issue/product visuals: use Total Complaints with Product, Sub-product,
-- Issue, Sub-issue as row/category, and suitable Top N filter.
-- 8. Period/month grouping: place Month Start on the X-axis and Total Complaints as values.
-- 9. Product-issue matrix: Product columns, Issue rows, Total Complaints values.
-- 10. Timeliness donut: filter legend Timely response? explicitly to only Yes/No.
-- 11. Public-response table: keep (Blank) as a distinct visible category.
-- Format *% measures as Percent (2 decimals); *Days measures as decimal days.
